{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JRSvWaV57gHKMnr6d2Ldi8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tid: srd066-expr\n2\ttitle: \"cmd/expr: Evaluate Expressions\"\n3\t\n4\tproblem: |\n5\t  Shell scripts use expr to evaluate integer arithmetic, string comparisons, string matching,\n6\t  and logical expressions from the command line. The macOS BSD expr differs from GNU expr in\n7\t  regex syntax and the + operator for string protection. The Go implementation must match the\n8\t  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gexpr, installed by coreutils) in output and exit codes for\n9\t  all supported operations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n10\t\n11\tgoals:\n12\t  - G1: Evaluate arithmetic, comparison, and logical expressions given as arguments.\n13\t  - G2: Support string matching and substring operations.\n14\t  - G3: Match GNU expr precedence, associativity, and output format.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Arithmetic and comparison operators\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"Must support integer arithmetic operators: + (add), - (subtract), * (multiply), / (integer divide), % (modulo). Each operator and operand is a separate argument.\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"Must support comparison operators: < (less), <= (less-equal), = (equal), != (not-equal), >= (greater-equal), > (greater). Comparisons on two integers use numeric comparison; otherwise use lexicographic comparison. Must return 1 for true and 0 for false.\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: \"Must support logical operators: | (or) returns the first argument if it is nonzero/non-empty, else the second; & (and) returns the first argument if both are nonzero/non-empty, else 0.\"\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"Must support parentheses for grouping: ( and ) override default precedence. Parentheses are separate arguments.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: String operations\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"match STRING REGEXP or STRING : REGEXP must anchor the pattern at the beginning of STRING and return the matched substring if the pattern contains \\\\( \\\\), or the number of matched characters otherwise.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: \"substr STRING POS LENGTH must return a substring of STRING starting at position POS (1-based) with length LENGTH.\"\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: \"index STRING CHARS must return the position (1-based) of the first character in STRING that is also in CHARS, or 0 if none.\"\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"length STRING must return the number of characters in STRING.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Special tokens and precedence\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: \"+ TOKEN must interpret TOKEN as a string even if it is a keyword (match, substr, index, length) or operator. The + is consumed and not part of the value.\"\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: \"Operator precedence from lowest to highest: | , & , comparisons (< <= = != >= >), + - (arithmetic), * / %.\"\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: \"All binary operators are left-associative.\"\n50\t      - R3.4:\n51\t          text: \"Division by zero must print an error to stderr and exit 2.\"\n52\t\n53\t  R4:\n54\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n55\t    items:\n56\t      - R4.1:\n57\t          text: \"Must exit 0 when the expression evaluates to a non-null, non-zero value.\"\n58\t      - R4.2:\n59\t          text: \"Must exit 1 when the expression evaluates to null or 0.\"\n60\t      - R4.3:\n61\t          text: \"Must exit 2 on syntax error (invalid expression, missing operand, division by zero). Must exit 3 on internal error.\"\n62\t      - R4.4:\n63\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr emptiness, and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: integer arithmetic (all operators), comparisons (numeric and string), logical operators, string operations (match, substr, index, length), parentheses, + escaping, division by zero, and missing operand errors.\"\n64\t\n65\tnon_goals:\n66\t  - cmd/expr does not implement GNU expr's --help and --version when they appear as the sole argument and could be confused with an expression operand.\n67\t  - cmd/expr does not implement arbitrary-precision arithmetic. Integer overflow behavior matches the host platform's int64 semantics.\n68\t  - cmd/expr does not implement extended regex. Only basic regular expressions (BRE) with \\\\( \\\\) grouping are supported.\n69\t\n70\tacceptance_criteria:\n71\t  - id: AC1\n72\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 2 + 3 prints '5' and exits 0, matching gexpr.\"\n73\t    traces:\n74\t      - R1.1\n75\t      - R4.1\n76\t  - id: AC2\n77\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 5 '<' 10 prints '1' and exits 0, matching gexpr.\"\n78\t    traces:\n79\t      - R1.2\n80\t      - R4.1\n81\t  - id: AC3\n82\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr match abcdef 'abc\\\\(.*\\\\)' prints 'def', matching gexpr.\"\n83\t    traces:\n84\t      - R2.1\n85\t  - id: AC4\n86\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr length hello prints '5', matching gexpr.\"\n87\t    traces:\n88\t      - R2.4\n89\t      - R4.1\n90\t  - id: AC5\n91\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 1 / 0 exits 2 with error on stderr, matching gexpr.\"\n92\t    traces:\n93\t      - R3.4\n94\t      - R4.3\n95\t  - id: AC6\n96\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gexpr passes for all cases listed in R4.4.\"\n97\t    traces:\n98\t      - R4.4\n99\t  - id: AC7\n100\t    criterion: \"cmd/expr compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n101\t    traces:\n102\t      - R1.1\n103\t      - R1.2\n104\t      - R1.3\n105\t      - R1.4\n106\t      - R2.1\n107\t      - R2.2\n108\t      - R2.3\n109\t      - R2.4\n110\t      - R3.1\n111\t      - R3.2\n112\t      - R3.3\n113\t      - R3.4\n114\t      - R4.1\n115\t      - R4.2\n116\t      - R4.3\n117\t      - R4.4\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"15282ba6-b144-470f-aec0-8eb1ee1c4d16","uuid":"8b7f3b6d-5089-4cc6-8f0b-1625e8c63886","timestamp":"2026-05-21T18:27:45.842Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5433/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd066-expr.yaml","content":"id: srd066-expr\ntitle: \"cmd/expr: Evaluate Expressions\"\n\nproblem: |\n  Shell scripts use expr to evaluate integer arithmetic, string comparisons, string matching,\n  and logical expressions from the command line. The macOS BSD expr differs from GNU expr in\n  regex syntax and the + operator for string protection. The Go implementation must match the\n  Homebrew GNU reference binary (gexpr, installed by coreutils) in output and exit codes for\n  all supported operations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Evaluate arithmetic, comparison, and logical expressions given as arguments.\n  - G2: Support string matching and substring operations.\n  - G3: Match GNU expr precedence, associativity, and output format.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Arithmetic and comparison operators\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"Must support integer arithmetic operators: + (add), - (subtract), * (multiply), / (integer divide), % (modulo). Each operator and operand is a separate argument.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"Must support comparison operators: < (less), <= (less-equal), = (equal), != (not-equal), >= (greater-equal), > (greater). Comparisons on two integers use numeric comparison; otherwise use lexicographic comparison. Must return 1 for true and 0 for false.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: \"Must support logical operators: | (or) returns the first argument if it is nonzero/non-empty, else the second; & (and) returns the first argument if both are nonzero/non-empty, else 0.\"\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"Must support parentheses for grouping: ( and ) override default precedence. Parentheses are separate arguments.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: String operations\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"match STRING REGEXP or STRING : REGEXP must anchor the pattern at the beginning of STRING and return the matched substring if the pattern contains \\\\( \\\\), or the number of matched characters otherwise.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"substr STRING POS LENGTH must return a substring of STRING starting at position POS (1-based) with length LENGTH.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"index STRING CHARS must return the position (1-based) of the first character in STRING that is also in CHARS, or 0 if none.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"length STRING must return the number of characters in STRING.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Special tokens and precedence\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"+ TOKEN must interpret TOKEN as a string even if it is a keyword (match, substr, index, length) or operator. The + is consumed and not part of the value.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"Operator precedence from lowest to highest: | , & , comparisons (< <= = != >= >), + - (arithmetic), * / %.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"All binary operators are left-associative.\"\n      - R3.4:\n          text: \"Division by zero must print an error to stderr and exit 2.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: \"Must exit 0 when the expression evaluates to a non-null, non-zero value.\"\n      - R4.2:\n          text: \"Must exit 1 when the expression evaluates to null or 0.\"\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"Must exit 2 on syntax error (invalid expression, missing operand, division by zero). Must exit 3 on internal error.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare stdout, stderr emptiness, and exit codes between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: integer arithmetic (all operators), comparisons (numeric and string), logical operators, string operations (match, substr, index, length), parentheses, + escaping, division by zero, and missing operand errors.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/expr does not implement GNU expr's --help and --version when they appear as the sole argument and could be confused with an expression operand.\n  - cmd/expr does not implement arbitrary-precision arithmetic. Integer overflow behavior matches the host platform's int64 semantics.\n  - cmd/expr does not implement extended regex. Only basic regular expressions (BRE) with \\\\( \\\\) grouping are supported.\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 2 + 3 prints '5' and exits 0, matching gexpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 5 '<' 10 prints '1' and exits 0, matching gexpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.2\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr match abcdef 'abc\\\\(.*\\\\)' prints 'def', matching gexpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.1\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr length hello prints '5', matching gexpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.1\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/expr 1 / 0 exits 2 with error on stderr, matching gexpr.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.3\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gexpr passes for all cases listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC7\n    criterion: \"cmd/expr compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R3.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":118,"startLine":1,"totalLines":118}}}
