{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user is executing a stitch task (#5433) for the go-unix-utils project. The task is to implement srd066-expr requirements R2.1-R2.4 (String operations) for the `cmd/expr` utility. Specifically:\n   - R2.1: `match STRING REGEXP` or `STRING : REGEXP` - anchor pattern at beginning, return matched substring if pattern contains `\\( \\)`, or number of matched characters otherwise\n   - R2.2: `substr STRING POS LENGTH` - return substring at 1-based POS with given LENGTH\n   - R2.3: `index STRING CHARS` - return 1-based position of first matching char, or 0\n   - R2.4: `length STRING` - return character count\n   \n   Files to modify: `cmd/expr/main.go` and `cmd/expr/expr_test.go`. Must preserve existing R1.1-R1.4 functionality. No git commands allowed. Must pass `go build`, `go vet`, and `go test`.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - GNU expr reimplementation in Go with differential testing against `gexpr` (Homebrew GNU coreutils)\n   - Basic Regular Expression (BRE) support with `\\( \\)` grouping\n   - Recursive descent parser for expression evaluation\n   - `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests` differential testing pattern\n   - `pkg/sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()` for SIGPIPE handling\n   - Operator precedence: `|` < `&` < comparisons < `+`/`-` < `*`/`/`/`%`\n   - The `:` operator is parsed at the same precedence level as `*`/`/`/`%` in `parseMulDiv()`\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - **docs/specs/software-requirements/srd066-expr.yaml**\n     - Source of truth for requirements. R2 (String operations) defines match, substr, index, length behaviors.\n     - Non-goals: no --help/--version, no arbitrary-precision arithmetic, no extended regex (BRE only with `\\( \\)`)\n     \n   - **cmd/expr/main.go** (existing, 403 lines)\n     - Already contains implementations for ALL string operations from R2.1-R2.4\n     - Key functions already present:\n       - `parseMatch()` (lines 338-347): handles `match STRING REGEXP` keyword form\n       - `evalMatch()` (lines 272-293): core match logic with BRE-to-Go-regex conversion, handles both group capture and character count return\n       - `parseSubstr()` (lines 349-376): handles `substr STRING POS LENGTH` with rune-based indexing\n       - `parseIndex()` (lines 378-393): handles `index STRING CHARS` with rune iteration\n       - `parseLength()` (lines 395-403): handles `length STRING` with rune count\n       - `breToGoRegex()` (lines 304-336): converts BRE patterns to Go regex syntax\n       - `hasGroup()` (lines 295-302): checks if pattern contains `\\(`\n       - The `:` operator is handled in `parseMulDiv()` (lines 176-179) at the `*`/`/`/`%` precedence level\n     - Parser structure: `parseOr()` → `parseAnd()` → `parseComparison()` → `parseAddSub()` → `parseMulDiv()` → `parsePrimary()`\n     - `parsePrimary()` dispatches keywords: match, substr, index, length, and handles `+` token escaping and parentheses\n     \n   - **cmd/expr/expr_test.go** (existing, 113 lines)\n     - Has differential tests for R1.1-R1.4 only (arithmetic, comparisons, logical operators, parentheses, division by zero, precedence)\n     - Uses `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` and `exec.LookPath(\"gexpr\")`\n     - Has a `normBinName` normalizer that replaces \"gexpr:\" with \"expr:\" in stderr\n     - **Does NOT have any tests for R2.1-R2.4** (match, substr, index, length)\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - No errors encountered yet. Was in the reading/analysis phase when interrupted.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Identified that the string operation code already exists in main.go but tests are missing\n   - Need to verify existing implementations are correct per SRD and add comprehensive differential tests\n   - Potential issue to verify: the `substr` function uses `p < 1 || l < 0 || p > len(runes)` guards - need to check this matches GNU behavior for edge cases\n   - The `:` infix operator for match is already handled in `parseMulDiv()` - need to add tests for this form too\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single massive user message containing the complete task specification with: role description, repository file listing, project context (vision, architecture, specifications, roadmap, analysis, requirement states), execution constitution, go style constitution, task description with requirements/design decisions/acceptance criteria, shared protocols, and package contracts.\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Verify existing R2.1-R2.4 implementations in `cmd/expr/main.go` are correct per SRD\n   - Add differential test cases to `cmd/expr/expr_test.go` covering:\n     - R2.1: match with `\\( \\)` groups (return substring), match without groups (return char count), `:` infix operator form, no-match cases\n     - R2.2: substr basic, edge cases (pos beyond string, length 0, etc.)\n     - R2.3: index basic, no-match returning 0, multiple matching chars\n     - R2.4: length basic, empty string, unicode\n   - Run `go build -o bin/expr ./cmd/expr/` to verify compilation\n   - Run `go vet ./cmd/expr/...` to check for issues\n   - Run `go test ./cmd/expr/... -count=1` to verify all tests pass\n   - Ensure existing R1.1-R1.4 tests continue to pass\n\n8. Current Work:\n   I had just finished reading all three required files (SRD, main.go, expr_test.go) and was about to begin the implementation phase. The analysis revealed that the string operation functions already exist in main.go, so the primary work is:\n   1. Review the existing implementations for correctness against the SRD\n   2. Add comprehensive differential test cases for R2.1-R2.4 to expr_test.go\n   3. Fix any implementation issues found during testing\n   4. Run build/vet/test verification\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the updated `cmd/expr/expr_test.go` with new test